From 5cbf25ad4d3b8fae51d76b454924de6cb46eb631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:00:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 48/82] OdfFile writer: a DOCX grid column is as wide as it
 says

Upstream's fix for bug 51597 added 37 twips to every grid column
narrower than 7 cm, to make up for cells that came back narrower after a
round trip. The reader writes a column's width to the twip, so the
addition widened every such column by 0.065 cm on every round trip: a
3 cm column read back as 3.066, 3.131, 3.196 cm on three trips. That is
drift in every document with a narrow table column; the fifth batch
exposed it in tdf150149.fodt. The width is now taken as written.

OdfFile writer: a zero-width grid column has no width

A DOCX grid column of width 0 became style:column-width="0cm", which
ODF does not allow. The 37 twips removed by the previous commit used to
turn it into 0.065 cm; deleted_table.fodt, whose table is a tracked
deletion, has one. It is now treated as a column without a width.

OdfFile writer: a zero cell width does not set its column's width

A DOCX cell of width 0 set its column's width to 0 when the grid gave
none, and ODF has no zero-width column: deleted_table.fodt, a tracked
table deletion, once the previous commit left its zero-width grid column
without a width. A cell width that is not positive is now ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp  | 16 +++++-----------
 OdfFile/Writer/Format/odf_table_context.cpp |  1 +
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp b/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
index 52d120f7ff..3356f68b53 100644
--- a/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
+++ b/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
@@ -4974,20 +4974,14 @@ void DocxConverter::convert(OOX::Logic::CTblGrid	*oox_table_grid, int columns_wi
 		if (oox_table_grid->m_arrGridCol[i] == NULL) continue;
 		double width = -1;
 
-		const double pt_per_cm = 28.3464567;
 
 		if (oox_table_grid->m_arrGridCol[i]->m_oW.IsInit())
 		{
-			if( oox_table_grid->m_arrGridCol[i]->m_oW->ToPoints() / pt_per_cm < 7.0 ) // check bug 51597
-			{
-				int twips = oox_table_grid->m_arrGridCol[i]->m_oW->ToTwips();
-				const double points = (twips + 37) / 20.0;
-				width = points;
-			}
-			else
-			{
-				width = oox_table_grid->m_arrGridCol[i]->m_oW->ToPoints();
-			}
+			// As written. Bug 51597 added 37 twips to every column under 7 cm, to make up for cells
+			// that came back narrower; the reader writes a column's width exactly, so each round trip
+			// widened such a column by 0.065 cm instead
+			width = oox_table_grid->m_arrGridCol[i]->m_oW->ToPoints();
+			if (width <= 0) width = -1; // no width: ODF has no zero-width column
 		}
 
 		odt_context->add_table_column(width);
diff --git a/OdfFile/Writer/Format/odf_table_context.cpp b/OdfFile/Writer/Format/odf_table_context.cpp
index 9fa2e18ec4..0a0f7e4169 100644
--- a/OdfFile/Writer/Format/odf_table_context.cpp
+++ b/OdfFile/Writer/Format/odf_table_context.cpp
@@ -491,6 +491,7 @@ void odf_table_context::set_column_optimal(bool val)
 void odf_table_context::change_current_column_width(double width)
 {
 	if (impl_->empty()) return;
+	if (width <= 0) return; // a cell without a width says nothing of its column's
 	
 	int index = impl_->current_table().current_column ;
 	if (index < 0) return;	
